One decision worth flagging: I did not add generic `toJSON` handling for arbitrary objects, only the behavior `JSON.stringify` already gives `Date` (and other non-plain objects) by leaving them untouched. A plain object with a custom `toJSON` would therefore have its keys sorted rather than calling `toJSON`, which was not part of the request.

